# Copy this file to .env in the .diffdata folder in your home folder, next to config.toml
# (C:\Users\<you>\.diffdata\.env on Windows, ~/.diffdata/.env on a Mac), and fill it in.
# Not in the repo folder: tools working in the repo, such as Codex, can read it there.
# Never commit real values, and never paste them into an Issue, PR or chat.
# Nothing reads these yet; DIS-6 (Issue #86) will be first.

# DIS-6: direct Slack API access (later; for now Claude's Slack connector does discovery)
SLACK_TOKEN=

# COL-4: the Google Docs sign-in doesn't use .env. Its client file goes in
# ~/.diffdata/google-client.json, outside the repo, and the sign-in is saved beside it.
